{"translation": "People know joys and sorrows, partings and reunions;
the moon is dim or bright, waxing and waning—
no such thing has ever been perfect since ancient times.
I only wish we may live long,
and share the same fair moon though a thousand miles apart.", "notes": ["From Su Shi's ci poem "Prelude to Water Melody," written in 1076 while separated from his brother.", ""Chan juan" (the fair moon) traditionally evokes the moon goddess and longing for absent loved ones."]}

